OROCHIMARU RESEARCH DIVISION
CURSED SEAL PROGRAM — VOLUME I: PRINCIPLE AND APPLICATION
CLEARANCE: RESEARCH CADRE

Abstract
The Cursed Seal is a means of transferring a fraction of the caster's chakra and will
into a recipient, where it lies dormant until the recipient's own chakra calls upon it.
Volume I documents the founding principle and the application procedure. Volume II covers
survival factors and long-term effects.

Principle
The seal is seeded by the caster's bite, delivering a concentrated dose of chakra bound
into a self-propagating mark. When the bearer draws on it, the mark spreads and floods
the body with borrowed power. The bearer's will is tested against the caster's; the
strong retain themselves, the weak are consumed.

Application
1. Subject is restrained; chakra reserve confirmed above threshold.
2. Seal delivered at the base of the neck or shoulder.
3. Subject enters acute crisis. This is the survival gate — most subjects expire here.
4. Survivors are stabilized, sealed with a suppression pattern, and entered to monitoring.

Preliminary Findings
- Survival correlates with intake chakra reserve and with force of will.
- Two seal variants (Heaven, Earth) show comparable survival but differ in transformation
  character. Continued in Volume II.

Filed by the Research Division under Lord Orochimaru's direction.
